# Milestone: v0.10.12-cat-e-activation
# Covers: determinism rule D-cross-2 — slot-change burst with 2 sync subs;
#         50 sequential obj.x = i writes; subscriber walk order is byte-stable
#         across 100x3 preset runs; D-slotchange-2 FIFO sub walk confirmed.
# blocked: T39 chk-runner tunables-extension (multi-preset mode) per
#          design-risks v0.10.7-G — the `at sync` keyword form ships
#          (Cat. E re-audit Cluster #15 verdict A reclassified the
#          original `at.sync` dot-syntax as a fixture-authoring error;
#          rewritten to keyword form below), but the 100x3-preset
#          determinism guarantee additionally requires the chk-runner
#          tunables-extension that hasn't shipped yet.
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Reason:
#   Requires Object.new() T69 stdlib binding and inline subscriber dispatch.
#   The deferred-slot-change ring (spec #4 §5.4) and sync subscriber walk
#   (FIFO walk of obj.x.changed_watchers_head) are tested by
#   test_slot_change_callsites.c and test_slot_change_reentrancy.c.
#
#   When active: 50 writes × 2 subs = 100 subscriber firings → 100-char log;
#   byte-identical across 100 runs under each of the 3 tunable presets.
#   Verifies D-slotchange-1 (program-order emit) + D-slotchange-2 (FIFO walk).
#
#   When v0.10.7-G ships: replace the source below with the activated
#   keyword-form variant.  The audit confirmed the C-level deferred-ring
#   drain + sync subscriber walk are tested by
#   test_slot_change_callsites.c and test_slot_change_reentrancy.c.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate when v0.10.7-G T39 ships):
#   var obj = Object.new();
#   var Realm.log = "";
#   at sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "A";
#   at sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "B";
#   var i = 0;
#   while (i < 50) { obj.x = i; Realm.i = i + 1 };
#   Realm.log
#   --- expected output (100 chars: 50 repetitions of "AB") ---
#   [00000001] "ABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABABAB"
